<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
           http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      Collapse the duplicate strategy column on trade_config back to the single
      column the JPA entity actually maps: stratergy_id (sic).

      How the duplicate happened
      ==========================
      A changeset '020_rename_stratergy_id_to_strategy_id' was applied to at
      least one database (recorded in DATABASECHANGELOG on 2026-06-02) and its
      file was later removed from the repo. It renamed stratergy_id ->
      strategy_id, but entity TradeConfig kept @Column(name="stratergy_id").
      With spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update, Hibernate then re-created
      stratergy_id as a fresh NULL column. Result on those databases:

        strategy_id   (renamed, holds the real values)
        stratergy_id  (Hibernate-made, entirely NULL)

      Every JPA read/write went to the NULL column, so TradeConfig.getStratergyId()
      returned null and StrategyFactory.execute() could not route. The native
      combined query only worked by accident, because SELECT tc.* happened to
      expose the old column at the ordinal the mapper expected.

      Why stratergy_id wins
      =====================
      It is what 003_create_trade_config_table.xml creates on a fresh database,
      what entity TradeConfig maps, and what every Java call site uses
      (StrategyFactory, OrderService, TradeConfigAdminService,
      EodDowntrendDetectionService). Renaming to the correct spelling is a
      separate, larger cleanup - it must move the entity field and all call
      sites together, and this changeset deliberately does not attempt it.

      Conditional by design
      =====================
      On a fresh database strategy_id never existed, so there is nothing to
      merge. The precondition marks this changeset as ran in that case instead
      of failing.
    -->
    <changeSet id="022_consolidate_strategy_id_on_trade_config" author="moneymaker">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <columnExists tableName="trade_config" columnName="strategy_id"/>
        </preConditions>

        <!-- Carry the real values over before the orphan column is removed.
             Only fills holes; never clobbers a non-null stratergy_id. -->
        <update tableName="trade_config">
            <column name="stratergy_id" valueComputed="strategy_id"/>
            <where>stratergy_id IS NULL AND strategy_id IS NOT NULL</where>
        </update>

        <dropColumn tableName="trade_config" columnName="strategy_id"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
